    "text": "To determine the total number of days John spent protesting, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of days John attended the first protest.\n2. Calculate the number of days he attended the second protest.\n3. Add the number of days from both protests to get the total.\n\nStep 1: John attended the first protest for 4 days.\n\nStep 2: The second protest lasted 25% longer than the first protest. To find out how many days the second protest lasted, we calculate 25% of 4 days and add it to 4 days.\n\\[ 25\\% \\text{ of } 4 = 0.25 \\times 4 = 1 \\text{ day} \\]\nSo, the second protest lasted:\n\\[ 4 + 1 = 5 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nStep 3: Add the number of days from both protests to get the total.\n\\[ 4 + 5 = 9 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of days John spent protesting is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
